//? Title: ITP: Actual Interpolation, Truncation and Projection
//? Subtitle: Matched callback histories, explicit tolerances and the n0 allowance
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Find a zero of a continuous scalar function from a sign-changing bracket while
controlling how many interval reductions may be needed. ITP combines an
interpolated guess with truncation and a projection that limits the worst-case
bracket width. We record all three stages from one executing solver, retain the
original cosine fixed-point example, and separate position tolerance from
function residual. The default n0=1 allows one extra worst-case trial; only n0=0
matches bisection's exact-arithmetic worst-case bound.
)
\toc

> A three-number example before the general rule

For f(x)=x cubed minus two on [0,2], endpoint values are −2 and six. The secant
interpolation gives 0.5. The midpoint is one and the truncation amount is 0.2
times width squared divided by initial width, or 0.4, so the truncated guess is
0.9. Set coordinate tolerance to 0.125 and n0=0: three halvings suffice in the
bisection bound, and the first projection radius is 0.125 times eight minus one,
which is zero. The actual evaluated coordinate is therefore one. The diagram
reads that recorded trial; no report-only implementation recomputes it.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/itp_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/itp_analysis.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <limits>
#include <cmath>
#include <stdexcept>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    const auto t = dm::algorithms::itp_trace([](double x) {
        return x * x * x - 2;
    }, 0, 2, {.125, 0, 100, 0});
    std::print("| trial | interpolate | delta | truncate | projection radius | actual x | f(x) |\n| ---: | " "---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &s : t.steps)
        if (s.projected)
            std::print("| {} | {:.8f} | {:.8f} | {:.8f} | {:.8f} | {:.8f} | {:.8f} |\n",
                       s.iteration, s.interpolated, s.delta, s.truncated,
                       s.projection_radius, s.x, s.f_x);
    std::print("Final root {:.8f}, stop {}, coordinate radius {:.8f}, projection trials {}, callbacks {}.\n",
               t.run.result.root, dm::algorithms::itp_stop_name(t.run.stop),
               t.run.radius, t.run.result.iterations, t.run.evaluations);
    dm::algorithms::itp_stage_diagram(t).save_svg("build/itp_tiny.svg");
}
```
