> Check interval geometry separately from small residuals

For a position-only experiment set residual_tolerance=0. Callback zeros still
stop, because their actual computed value is zero. The next figure compares
pre-evaluation half-widths on the same cosine problem; these are not candidate
radii when a projected point lies off centre. The returned run radius is the
maximum distance from its actual estimate to either endpoint.

We also scan six coordinate tolerances, both n0 settings and four fixed
sign-transition locations in [0,1]. Their callbacks return only −1 and +1, so
there is no callback zero or residual acceptance to hide interval work. These
finite discontinuous controls test bracket geometry and trial budgets; they have
no mathematical root, so they are not examples of root existence. Observed
maxima over four locations are a bounded control, not an exhaustive worst-case
proof; that role belongs to the projection argument above.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/itp_width.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/itp_analysis.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <limits>
#include <cmath>
#include <stdexcept>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    std::print("| tolerance exponent k | n0 | theoretical allowance | maximum trials over four locations | " "projection-limit stops |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (int k : {6, 12, 18, 24, 30, 36})
        for (int n0 : {0, 1}) {
            int maximum = 0, limited = 0, bound = 0;
    for (double location : {.031, .173, .731, .971}) {
        const auto r = dm::algorithms::itp_run([location](double x) {
            return x < location ? -1. : 1.;
        }, 0, 1, {std::ldexp(1., -k), 0, 100, n0});
        maximum = std::max(maximum, r.result.iterations);
        bound = r.projection_bound;
        limited += r.stop == dm::algorithms::ItpStop::ProjectionLimit;
        if (r.result.iterations > bound)
            throw std::runtime_error("projection allowance violated");
    }
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", k, n0, bound, maximum, limited);
        }
        const auto f = [](double x) { return std::cos(x) - x; };
        const auto a = dm::algorithms::itp_trace(f, 0, 1, {1e-12, 0});
        const auto b =
            dm::algorithms::bisection_trace(f, 0, 1, {1e-12, 0, 100});
        std::print("Position-only cosine: ITP {} projection trials and {} callbacks; bisection {} midpoint " "trials and {} callbacks.\n",
                   a.run.result.iterations, a.run.evaluations,
                   b.result.iterations, b.evaluations);
        dm::algorithms::itp_bisection_plot(a, b).title("Position-only cosine: actual pre-evaluation bracket half-widths").ylim(-19, 2).save_svg("build/itp_width.svg");
}
